WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:55.430
<b>The Hundred-Million Man</b>

3
00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.000
[LUFFY]
Something's wrong
with these things!

4
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.500
They aren't normal!

5
00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.380
[screams]

6
00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.050
What's wrong with this forest?

7
00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.460
Duuuuu!

8
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.470
[CHOPPER]
It's his fault!

9
00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.390
[LUFFY]
Whose?

10
00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:32.300
[CHOPPER]
The South Bird!

11
00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.640
It's him! He's
controlling the bugs!

12
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.850
[LUFFY]
He can control
bugs and guide ships?

13
00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.020
Shh! Quiet.

14
00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.180
You guys hear anything?

15
00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:53.890
Somethin'.

16
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.970
But it sure doesn't
sound like any bird to me.

17
00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:57.910
Up there!

18
00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.140
[SANJI]
What the...?

19
00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.760
What are they? Boulders?

20
00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.760
Yeah, it looks
like an avalanche!

21
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.250
No, you're wrong! They're bugs!

22
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.090
[SANJI]
Ladybugs!

23
00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.210
[USOPP]
Big ones!

24
00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.580
Heh heh heh! Heh heh heh!

25
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.850
[ZORO]
Ugh.

26
00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.040
There's no end to them!

27
00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.960
They just keep popping up!

28
00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.690
Stupid crickets!

29
00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:23.060
Oh come on! You think
you can beat me? Do ya?

30
00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.880
[SOUTH BIRD]
Duuuuu!

31
00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:25.810
[ROBIN]
I wish those birds

32
00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.110
were as easy to see
as they are to hear.

33
00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.320
[SANJI]
A slug that
size needs a lot of salt!

34
00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.730
How can you think of
cooking at a time like this?

35
00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.690
[SANJI]
I'm not,
salt dissolves slugs, idiot!

36
00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.340
I'm sick of all this running!

37
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.990
Let's stand and fight!

38
00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.010
Come on, you bugs, bring it on!

39
00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:42.800
[CHOPPER]
No, Luffy!

40
00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.820
Just one sting
and you're history!

41
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.070
[USOPP]
Fireflies!

42
00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:47.650
[NAMI]
Pretty!

43
00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.570
Eww! Roaches!

44
00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:50.500
[USOPP]
Pigs!

45
00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.170
Yeah!

46
00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.670
[giggles]

47
00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.420
[laughs]

48
00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.460
So whaddaya think about

49
00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.010
We hit the jackpot!

50
00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:03.180
Oh! I'll say!

51
00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.140
Look at this!

52
00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.940
That's a fine piece of gold!

53
00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.630
[CRICKET]
Huh? No way.

54
00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.860
You punks have no
right to take that gold!

55
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:14.510
[SARQUISS]
Huh?

56
00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.530
No right?

57
00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.600
I'll show ya what
gives us the right!

58
00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:23.440
Big Chop!

59
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.870
Oh, you damn fool!

60
00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:32.920
We're way stronger than you
and your pals, old man!

61
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.650
I'd say that alone gives us
the right to take what we want,

62
00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.780
when we want, don't you?

63
00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.260
Come on! Let's dance!

64
00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.080
If you don't mind,
I'm cutting in!

65
00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.230
Havoc sonar!

66
00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:50.450
[wails]

67
00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:56.670
Lousy!

68
00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.800
[BELLAMY]
Sarquiss, no!

69
00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.660
I'm going to finish him
off my way!

70
00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:04.680
It's him again.

71
00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.910
The one with those
Spring‐Spring fruit powers.

72
00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.800
Shojo, run,
get out of there now!

73
00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.090
[BELLAMY]
Spring...

74
00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:14.180
[wails]

75
00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:15.850
[BELLAMY]
...Sniper!

76
00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:20.260
No! Shojo!

77
00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.020
[SHOJO]
Old‐timer! Look what we found!

78
00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.190
Gold! A bell‐shaped ingot!

79
00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.650
[laughs]

80
00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.580
[MASIRA]
Look! It's just like
it says here in the logbook!

81
00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.580
Gold bells!

82
00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.580
The story's true!

83
00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.800
[BELLAMY]
We're done here. Load up! Let's go!

84
00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.450
And as for you,
old man, grow up!

85
00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.390
[laughs]

86
00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.890
This "City of Gold"
is just a fairytale!

87
00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.230
That liar, Noland,
dreamt it all up!

88
00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.800
If you want to be
a pirate in this new era,

89
00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.270
you've got to wise up.

90
00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.770
Your dreams will
never come true! Ever!

91
00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.310
[laughter]

92
00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.940
[MASIRA]
The City of Gold
does exist! Hehe!

93
00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.290
[CRICKET laughs]
Hey, guys! Take it easy!

94
00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.750
My house is pretty small!

95
00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.000
Ya know something, junior?

96
00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:38.090
[coughs]

97
00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.430
A worthless little punk like you
who is too afraid to believe

98
00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:53.190
in dreams doesn't have the
right to call himself a pirate.

99
00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:55.100
What was that?

100
00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.600
[ZORO]
It's like trying
to find a needle in a haystack.

101
00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:06.810
We didn't even see one.

102
00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.690
[LUFFY]
Well, we did, but we
could never get close enough

103
00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:12.190
to grab it thanks
to all those stupid bugs.

104
00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:14.330
All we did was run.

105
00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.810
So seven people
couldn't catch one bird?

106
00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:17.800
That's pathetic!

107
00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.720
C'mon would you
get it together, guys!

108
00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.100
You're one to talk.

109
00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.070
[sighs]
We've been doing this for hours!

110
00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.820
I don't think I can run anymore!

111
00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:28.670
Duuuuu!

112
00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.800
Du du du du du! Duu duu!

113
00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.440
He just said, "You
morons think you can catch us?

114
00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.020
Hah! Good one!"

115
00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.480
Morons? What nerve!

116
00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.980
Hey, birdbrain,
I'll give you a "good one,"

117
00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:42.240
right between your eyes!

118
00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.570
Duu! Duu!

119
00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.740
[ROBIN]
I can grab it if I can see it.

120
00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.940
Duuuuu!

121
00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.200
[LUFFY]
Hey, Pops!

122
00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.330
We caught one of those birds!

123
00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.830
Pops! What happened?

124
00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.570
[USOPP]
Masira!

125
00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.820
[SANJI]
Shojo!

126
00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:06.610
[NAMI]
What the...?

127
00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:07.940
What happened here?

128
00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.570
[SANJI]
I've got a better question.

129
00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.640
Who did this?

130
00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.330
Hey, gimme a hand!

131
00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.770
[USOPP]
Aahh! The Going Merry!

132
00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.440
What happened to her?

133
00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.270
Who did this?

134
00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.770
When I find out,
they're gonna be sorry

135
00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:22.280
they ever laid a finger
on her, the savages!

136
00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.530
Dammit!

137
00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:24.400
[CRICKET]
Sorry, kid.

138
00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.560
You're alive!

139
00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:27.930
– Don't try to move, okay?
– I'm really sorry about this.

140
00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:29.680
– Just take it easy!
– I'm really sorry about this.

141
00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:32.850
We did everything we could to
stop them, but it wasn't enough.

142
00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.410
They made us
look pretty pathetic.

143
00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:37.400
We gotta get movin' though.

144
00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.740
Your ship's not
gonna patch itself up.

145
00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.540
Hold on, Pops. Wait!
Tell us what happened first!

146
00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:44.230
Who did this to you?

147
00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:44.980
Calm down.

148
00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:45.850
It's okay.

149
00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:46.980
Don't worry about it.

150
00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:48.970
It doesn't matter anymore.

151
00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.470
Did you have any
luck finding a...

152
00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.600
Duuu.

153
00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.020
Look at that,
you got yourself a South Bird.

154
00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.680
Nice job.

155
00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.140
They're hard to catch.

156
00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:00.720
[NAMI]
Luffy!

157
00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:01.420
Huh?

158
00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:04.390
Cricket's gold! It's all gone!

159
00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:10.480
That stuff?

160
00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.190
It's junk.

161
00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.320
Just forget it.

162
00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.440
It doesn't matter.

163
00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:15.310
Your dream is more important.

164
00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.860
We have to get
you to the Knock...

165
00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.860
Forget it?
How can you say that?

166
00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.570
Think about what it
took to get that gold!

167
00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.480
Ten years of diving to
the bottom of the ocean!

168
00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.940
Subjecting your body to all
the pressures of the deep!

169
00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.700
Shut up!

170
00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:31.570
I'm serious.

171
00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:34.460
That gold, and what
happens to it, is our problem.

172
00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:36.380
Got it?

173
00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:39.380
Your ship's in no shape to
make it to the Knock‐Up Stream.

174
00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.590
If we can get all the
Saruyama Alliance crew here,

175
00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:44.810
they'll have it fixed
and reinforced by morning.

176
00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.810
You'll still be able
to set sail tomorrow.

177
00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:49.590
Listen.

178
00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.390
Everything will be all right.

179
00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:54.220
We will send you to the sky,
I promise that.

180
00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.850
Old‐timer.

181
00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.370
Hey, Luffy.

182
00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:07.250
That's Bellamy's mark!

183
00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.240
You want any help?

184
00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:12.660
I'll handle this one alone.

185
00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:13.980
[NAMI]
Luffy, don't be stupid!

186
00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.490
We don't have time for this!

187
00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:18.330
We have to set
sail in three hours!

188
00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:22.770
[LUFFY]
If I follow the coast,

189
00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.440
will that take me all the
way back to Mock Town?

190
00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:27.040
Yes, I believe it will.

191
00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:32.450
Hey, where are you goin'?

192
00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.700
Don't be an idiot!

193
00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:37.290
You can't possibly take on this
Bellamy guy all by yourself!

194
00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:39.580
If you wanna stop him, use this.

195
00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:42.840
Kid. Don't do it.

196
00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:49.250
I'll be back by morning, guys.

197
00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.760
[DRUNKARD taking a leak]

198
00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.120
Well, lookee there!

199
00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:56.040
Wow! Looks like the ole moon's
right out there under the water!

200
00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.880
Guess my eyesight's
really gettin' bad!

201
00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:00.390
I better get my eyes checked

202
00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:03.590
or I'm gonna end up
fallin' off this dock!

203
00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.970
Hahah!

204
00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:05.680
Imagine that!

205
00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.930
A pirate with bad eyesight!

206
00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.060
Me?

207
00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.900
I think I'd rather lose one eye
than have two bad ones!

208
00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:12.960
Hahah.

209
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.420
'Least I'd get an eyepatch!

210
00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.630
[laughs]

211
00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:18.590
A fancy one, too!

212
00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:19.470
Hey!

213
00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:20.630
Whadda ya know!

214
00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:21.440
A newspaper!

215
00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:25.610
It must be the
really early edition!

216
00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.360
Huh? This ain't no paper!

217
00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.650
It's a stack of wanted posters!

218
00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:30.800
Oh, boy.

219
00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.410
What is this town comin'
to when low‐life scum outnumber

220
00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:36.460
the fine, upstanding
citizens like myself?

221
00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.500
Huh?

222
00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:40.640
It's those spineless guys
from this afternoon!

223
00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:41.560
Hah!

224
00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.440
That looney kid talkin'
about the island

225
00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.440
in the sky was a riot!

226
00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:46.610
What was he worth?

227
00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:49.060
Thirty million? Hmm?

228
00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:50.630
[laughs]

229
00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.840
I guess my eyesight really
is gettin' pretty bad!

230
00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.880
So one, ten, one hundred,
one thousand,

231
00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:02.180
ten thousand,
one hundred thousand?

232
00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:06.480
I think I'm gonna need
some reading glasses!

233
00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:08.940
One hundred thousand.

234
00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:11.940
O‐One million.

235
00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:17.150
One hundred million?

236
00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:22.570
[NAMI]
Three hours, Luffy!

237
00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.490
That's all you've got!

238
00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:28.500
If you take any longer...

239
00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:34.130
[NAMI]
...we're going to lose
our chance to go to sky island,

240
00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:37.050
and it's going to
be all your fault!

241
00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.180
He's in bad shape!

242
00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:40.350
It looks like he's been diving
dangerously like this for years,

243
00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.600
coming up too quick,

244
00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:44.980
and not giving the gas bubbles
enough time to fully dissipate!

245
00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.360
All I'm doing is
following what I believe

246
00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:50.810
to be my destiny.

247
00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.810
This is a battle
between me and Noland.

248
00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.900
I'm really sorry kid.

249
00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:02.740
We did what we could to stop
them but it wasn't enough.

250
00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.620
[LUFFY]
Bellamy!

251
00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.360
[SARQUISS]
Those apes really cracked me up!

252
00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:15.280
It was hilarious when they
were all bloody and had tears

253
00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.110
and snot runnin'
all down their faces,

254
00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:20.700
and started cryin', "Old‐timer!"

255
00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:22.620
[laughs]

256
00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:23.780
If he really meant so much,

257
00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.290
they should have done a
better job of protecting him!

258
00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:27.030
Right?

259
00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.330
Yeah, those guys were so lame!

260
00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.830
[laughs]

261
00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.290
Hey, what did you expect?

262
00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.210
The same thing would
have happened

263
00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.470
to anyone else
as stupid as them!

264
00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:37.220
Taking on a big‐time pirate
worth 55 million Berries

265
00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.430
like Bellamy?

266
00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:39.890
That's just insane!

267
00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.260
[DRUNKARD]
Bad news!

268
00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:45.390
[PATRON A]
This better be good.

269
00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:48.700
Those guys!

270
00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:49.990
The ones that were
here this afternoon!

271
00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.620
They...

272
00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:52.790
Bellamy!

273
00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.760
What on Earth are
you still doing here?

274
00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:59.970
You... You've gotta get outta here this instant!
I'm serious! You're in terrible danger!

275
00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:02.810
Tch! What are
you talking about?

276
00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:05.020
How am I in danger?

277
00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:33.240
Those two together
are worth a 160 million!

278
00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.200
Their bounties are higher
than yours, Bellamy!

279
00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:35.910
Know what that means?

280
00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:37.580
You're dead meat!

281
00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.580
And so are we!

282
00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.980
We were laughing at them!

283
00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.770
I think we messed
with the wrong people!

284
00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:43.980
They'll kill us!

285
00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.400
Ya think they
remember what we look like?

286
00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.820
We should get out of here!

287
00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.150
Now!

288
00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.280
I've never heard of anyone

289
00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:54.740
having a bounty
worth 100 million before.

290
00:14:54.780 --> 00:15:00.330
[BELLAMY laughs]

291
00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.080
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

292
00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.630
All it takes to scare
you big, tough guys

293
00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.880
are some little scraps of paper?

294
00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.210
What, do you all have
empty sockets for eyes?

295
00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.130
You saw their
scrawny, little leader!

296
00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.640
[LUFFY]
Made it!

297
00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:16.260
This is nothing but a sham!

298
00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.220
Here, I'll explain
it to you morons!

299
00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:20.290
See, there are pirates
like these losers who fake

300
00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:24.210
their own wanted posters just
to make a name for themselves!

301
00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.190
The fakers win fights
without throwing a single punch!

302
00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:30.210
Their enemies take one look at
the bogus bounties, turn tail,

303
00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.220
and run just like
you sorry excuses for pirates

304
00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.660
are doing right now!

305
00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.280
You saw them! They're weak!

306
00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:37.640
They didn't even fight back!

307
00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.670
But now you're all scared.

308
00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.230
Pathetic!

309
00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:42.190
Thanks, Bellamy!

310
00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:44.900
Hey, they almost pulled
one over on us, huh?

311
00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:45.980
Yeah, he's right!

312
00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.140
Besides, someone with a
bounty of 100 million would

313
00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:50.360
have had to have pulled off
some pretty big capers.

314
00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:52.270
He looked pretty young,
if you ask me.

315
00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:53.480
And if that kid's so wanted,

316
00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:56.280
how come we've never seen his
picture in the papers before?

317
00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.440
Good point.

318
00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:00.280
I've never heard of any kid
in a straw hat, have you?

319
00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.200
[PATRON A]
I got to admit!

320
00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:04.200
I was pretty scared
there for a moment!

321
00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.070
[LUFFY]
Bellamy!

322
00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.650
Where are you?

323
00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:29.330
Heh. Excuse me, gentlemen.

324
00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.680
[LUFFY]
Hey!

325
00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:45.930
Well, speak of the devil.

326
00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:48.060
We were just talking about you.

327
00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:51.270
You got something
you wanna say to me, kid?

328
00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:52.190
I do.

329
00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:55.490
Give back Pops' gold!
Every bit of it! Right now!
